body:
`MutationProcessor::process` was using per-thread partitioning (`calcSystemThreadPartition`) with 8 threads/block, meaning each thread sequentially iterated all 16 neurons × 16 weights per node. Rewrites to block-level parallelism so an entire CUDA block cooperates on genome mutation.

### MutationProcessor rewrite

- `process()` uses `calcBlockPartition`; thread 0 handles `atomicCAS` + genome clone, all threads cooperate on mutations via `block.sync()`
- `applyMutations_neurons()` parallelizes the neuron loop: each of `NEURONS_PER_CELL` (16) threads handles one neuron independently
- Kernel launch changed from `STREAM_KERNEL_CALL` (8 threads) to `STREAM_KERNEL_CALL_MOD` with `NEURONS_PER_CELL` threads/block

```cuda
// Before: single thread does all 16 neurons sequentially
for (int neuronIndex = 0; neuronIndex < NEURONS_PER_CELL; ++neuronIndex) {
    if (isRandomEvent(data, rate.probability)) { ... }
}

// After: each thread owns one neuron
if (laneId < NEURONS_PER_CELL) {
    int neuronIndex = laneId;
    if (isRandomEvent(data, rate.probability)) { ... }
}
```

### clang-format include reordering fix

- `IncludeBlocks: Regroup` → `Preserve` — prevents cross-block reordering that broke CUDA compilation due to transitive include-order dependencies
- Extended CUDA headers regex to cover `cooperative_groups.*`, `sm_*`, `device_launch_parameters.h`
- Extended local includes regex to match `.cuh` files (was `.h` only)
- Added missing direct includes to `MuscleProcessor.cuh` (`ConstantMemory.cuh`, `ObjectConnectionProcessor.cuh`) that were only satisfied transitively

